<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrés Bonifacio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a>–<a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Andres Bonifacio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrés Bonifacio was a Filipino revolutionary who co-founded the Katipunan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in 1892 and became its supreme leader. He launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution">Philippine Revolution</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in August 1896. After a power struggle with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a>'s faction, he was tried and executed by fellow revolutionaries in May 1897.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andres-bonifacio.jpg" alt="Andrés Bonifacio" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chofre y Cia (now Cacho Hermanos Inc.) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andr%C3%A9s_Bonifacio_photo_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
